SQL is asked in nearly every interview, and for backend and data roles it is absolutely essential. Learn it
with PostgreSQL, because that is what you will use with FastAPI.

Topics: SELECT, WHERE, ORDER BY, LIMIT, aggregate functions, GROUP BY and HAVING, all
types of JOINs, subqueries, CTEs (WITH clause), window functions (ROW_NUMBER, RANK, LAG,
LEAD), CASE WHEN, constraints and keys, indexes, normalization up to 3NF, transactions and ACID
properties.

• Learn: SQLBolt (sqlbolt.com) for the basics in a day or two, then PostgreSQL Tutorial
(postgresqltutorial.com).
• Practise: the LeetCode SQL 50 study plan on leetcode.com, HackerRank SQL track, and SQLZoo
(sqlzoo.net).
• GitHub: repo named sql_practice with one .sql file per topic, plus a small database design of your
own (for example a college library) with a diagram in the README.
• Done when: you can find the second highest salary in each department, explain the difference
between WHERE and HAVING, and design tables for a simple app without help.
